+# BLUE CURRENT V50.20.0 — PRODUCTION RECOVERY & POST-INCIDENT REVIEW
+
+V50.16–V50.20 adds the recovery-verification and lessons-learned layer after a human-resolved production incident.
+
+## Recovery verification
+
+Resolved incidents are evaluated against current production state.
+
+For each affected restaurant Blue Current checks:
+
+1. Production support health is not critical.
+2. Restaurant readiness is at least 70.
+3. No open critical production support event remains.
+
+If no location-specific scope exists, platform reliability is used as the recovery signal.
+
+The review also summarizes:
+
+- incident start / resolution time
+- incident duration in minutes
+- business impact
+- service impact
+- incident commander
+- human resolution
+- recovery evidence
+- current platform SLO/reliability state
+
+## Human-authored post-incident review
+
+Adds:
+
+POST `/api/production-recovery-review/incidents/:incidentId/review`
+
+A review requires:
+
+- human-authored root cause
+- at least one corrective action
+- corrective-action owner
+- repeat-risk assessment
+- executive post-incident summary
+
+Optional contributing factors are captured explicitly.
+
+Repeat risk:
+
+- low
+- medium
+- high
+- critical
+
+## Corrective actions
+
+Each corrective action records:
+
+- action
+- owner
+- due date
+- status: `OPEN`
+- execution state: `NOT_EXECUTED_BY_BLUE_CURRENT`
+
+Blue Current records corrective work but does not execute it.
+
+Each review also explicitly records:
+
+- `correctiveActionsExecutedBySystem: false`
+- `runtimeMutationPerformed: false`
+
+## Human lessons acceptance
+
+Adds:
+
+POST `/api/production-recovery-review/reviews/:reviewId/accept-lessons`
+
+Acceptance is admin-only and requires:
+
+- named approver
+- human closure / lessons note
+
+Accepted state:
+
+`POST_INCIDENT_REVIEW_ACCEPTED`
+
+## Executive review record
+
+The stored post-incident review provides the decision-ready executive record:
+
+- duration
+- impact
+- recovery status
+- root cause
+- contributing factors
+- corrective actions / owners / due dates
+- repeat risk
+- executive summary
+- lessons acceptance
+- closure note
+
+## Safety policy
+
+- `recoveryVerificationReadOnly: true`
+- `rootCauseHumanAuthored: true`
+- `correctiveActionsHumanOwned: true`
+- `lessonsAcceptanceHumanRequired: true`
+- `automaticCorrectiveActionExecution: false`
+- `automaticClosure: false`
+- `autonomousProductionChanges: false`
+
+## Current authenticated runtime
+
+The untouched Chefs runtime has no human-resolved production incident yet.
+
+V50.20 therefore correctly reports:
+
+- status: `resolved-incident-required`
+- resolved incidents in post-incident review: 0
+- automatic corrective-action execution: false
+- automatic closure: false
+- autonomous production changes: false
+
+The current demo owner account does not have the admin permission used to accept post-incident lessons, and an attempted acceptance correctly returns HTTP 403.
+
+## Validation
+
+- V50.20 Production Recovery & Post-Incident Review lifecycle PASS
+- restored-service verification PASS
+- affected-location recovery state PASS
+- incident duration / impact summary PASS
+- human root-cause capture PASS
+- contributing-factor capture PASS
+- corrective actions + ownership PASS
+- repeat-risk assessment PASS
+- executive summary PASS
+- human lessons acceptance PASS
+- corrective actions remain NOT_EXECUTED_BY_BLUE_CURRENT PASS
+- V50.15 Production Incident Command regression PASS
+- authenticated recovery-review GET PASS
+- admin lessons-acceptance boundary PASS
+- authoritative database unchanged
+- npm run check PASS
+- 911 JavaScript files
+- 766 client scripts
+- 5,724 unique HTML IDs
+
+## Next
+
+V50.21–V50.25 should build Production Learning & Corrective Action Governance:
+
+- corrective-action register across incidents
+- action owner / due-date aging
+- overdue / high-risk corrective work
+- repeat-incident linkage
+- risk-reduction evidence
+- executive accountability rollup
+- action verification
+- human completion / acceptance
+- no automatic corrective-action execution
